      <button class="implementation-back" type="button" disabled data-view="implementation">← Implementation guide</button>
      <div class="design-heading"><span class="badge design">PROPOSED ARCHITECTURE</span><h2>Stable behavior. Explicit authority.</h2><p>A local model proposes. Independent software checks permission, advances the workflow, and records the outcome.</p></div>
      <div class="authority-flow" aria-label="Proposed control flow"><div><span>01 / COMMUNICATION</span><strong>Scientist persona</strong><p>Warmth, clarity, scientific care.</p></div><div><span>02 / CONTEXT</span><strong>Revisable memory</strong><p>Evidence, scope, conflicts, expiry.</p></div><div class="authority-node"><span>03 / ENFORCEMENT</span><strong>Permission &amp; state</strong><p>Authenticated authority. Exact action checks.</p></div><div><span>04 / OUTCOME</span><strong>Verified receipt</strong><p>Attempted, completed, or unknown.</p></div></div>
      <div class="design-grid"><section><div class="section-label">DESIGN REQUIREMENTS</div><div id="principles"></div></section><section><div class="section-label">QUESTIONS TO RESOLVE</div><div id="questions"></div></section></div>
      <div class="experiment"><div><span class="section-label">FIRST COMPARISON</span><h3>One frozen model. Three configurations.</h3><p>Fixed persona → reviewed examples → curated case memory.</p></div><div><strong>Measure separately</strong><p>Personality · factual accuracy · authorized completion · false denials · unauthorized proposals · executed effects.</p></div></div>
    </section>
